TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R5","met":"yes","where":"Useful Links"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Ocean acidification is presented as the cause of coral bleaching. Bleaching is driven mainly by thermal stress, so the causal chain is misstated."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The claim that current satellites map GBR depths only to 100 m per pixel is unreferenced and may be inaccurate; the cited source does not support a direct comparison with the proposed mission."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"Mission requirements are absent: no orbit regime, altitude, payload, coverage or latency target is given, so the concept cannot be linked to space-segment design."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The statement that hundreds of millions of humans rely on reefs is unreferenced, and the 30% acidity figure is loosely phrased without the pH or H+ basis."}],"overall":"A sensible, Australia-focused reef-monitoring concept with a feasible Gantt plan and a reasonable reference set. Weaknesses are the lack of stated mission requirements and orbit/space-segment linkage, very thin technical progress, a causal error on acidification and bleaching, and minor inconsistencies in referencing and figure captioning.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The purpose (monitoring GBR bleaching), the Australian benefit, and the primary users (marine and conservation scientists) are clear and supported by footnoted sources. However, mission goals, objectives and quantified requirements are not stated, and the functional link to the space segment is thin. Other users such as reef managers are not identified. Some claims are unreferenced, so this sits at Adequate.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Coral reefs, specifically the Great Barrier Reef, would immensely benefit from dedicated satellite monitoring."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events"}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":18.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"A week-by-week Gantt chart covers all major tasks with dates, status colours and task descriptions, and it is clearly feasible. Information sources are listed as links. However, there is no explicit contingency or variation provision for slipped tasks, and the plan is not tied explicitly to the mission narrative. Adequate fits best.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Project work will be divided into weeks via a Gantt Chart."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Week 10 is reserved for review, amendments, final simulations, and reflection."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Adequate","mark":4.0,"scale":10.0,"points":4.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"Work to date is limited to literature review, reading a bleaching-monitoring brief and completing STK tutorials. No technical results are presented, such as orbit parameters, coverage, ground-track or link calculations, or STK outputs. Progress is minor and cannot yet be judged as clearly on track, so Adequate low is appropriate.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"and also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Accomplished","mark":7.0,"scale":10.0,"points":14.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"Structure is logical with clear headings, writing is mostly fluent and the Gantt chart is readable. Footnote citations are used. However, the Gantt chart has no figure caption, the red deadline lines are hard to see, the footnotes and Useful Links list do not map one-to-one, and some wording is informal or awkward.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Completed stages are gold. Incomplete stages are blue."},{"where":"Useful Links","quote":"Useful Links"}]}]}
